# ExecuteURML — run a URML program (or a natural-language sentence) through
# URML's validate-before-actuate pipeline, served as a ROS 2 action.
#
# A behavior engine (FlexBE, BehaviorTree.CPP, a custom orchestrator) sends a
# goal; the URML action server validates it against the robot's capability
# manifest + safety envelope, refuses with a verdict if it does not hold, and
# otherwise executes it against the substrate adapter (Nav2 / MoveIt 2 / ...).
#
# Exactly one of `program_yaml` / `sentence` drives the run: a program is
# executed as-is; a sentence is translated to URML first (requires an LLM
# provider configured on the server). YAML payloads are passed as strings so
# this interface needs no URML-specific message types.

# --- Goal ---
string program_yaml        # a URML program (YAML/JSON). Empty if using `sentence`.
string sentence            # natural-language request. Empty if using `program_yaml`.
string manifest_yaml       # the robot's capability manifest (YAML/JSON). Required.
string envelope_yaml       # optional safety envelope (YAML/JSON). Empty for none.
string[] profiles          # active URML profiles (e.g. ["home"]).
bool no_policy             # skip the compliance policy pass (hero-demo path).
---
# --- Result ---
bool success               # true iff every step executed successfully.
bool refused               # true iff validation rejected the program (no actuation).
string reason              # rendered verdict on refusal, or last-step reason.
int32 steps_executed       # number of primitives actually dispatched.
string audit_log_json      # the runtime audit trail, JSON-encoded.
string bindings_json       # final variable bindings, JSON-encoded.
---
# --- Feedback ---
string phase               # "translating" | "validating" | "executing" | "done".
string detail              # short human-readable status for the operator UI.
